<title>USA: Pacificorp unit sells cellular holdings.</title>
<headline>Pacificorp unit sells cellular holdings.</headline>
<dateline>PORTLAND, Ore 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pacificorp's Pacific Telecom Inc signed a letter of intent with Century Telephone Enterprises Inc to exchange the stock of Pacific Telecom Cellular Inc for $164.4 million in cash and more than 18,000 of Century's telephone access lines in Arizona, Colorado, Idaho and New Mexico.</p>
<p>Upon completion of all pending transactions, Pacific Telecom will provide service to about 660,000 access lines, making Pacific Telecom the 15th largest local exchange telephone company, based on access lines in the United States.</p>
</text>
